      "writtenOn": "2022-10-06T05:26:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what you mean (lets chat tomorrow), my current thinking is:\n\n1. `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_SPI_FLASH_REG` exists in common/spi/flash_reg/Kconfig.module and will generate the `spi_flash_reg` library\n2. `CONFIG_CROS_FLASH_NPCX` enables building `cros_flash_npcx.c` but it also needs to link `spi_flash_reg` so here I\u0027m using `sources_ifdef` and `link_libraries_ifdef` keyed on the same config.\n\nNote that `CROS_FLASH_NPCX` includes a `select PLATFORM_EC_FLASH_CROS` so we\u0027re sure that the library exists.\n\nPigweed has some nice utilities where they include all the sources and dependencies in the same cmake function, for us it will look something like:\n\n```\ncros_module(module_name\n  SOURCES\n    cros_flash_npcx.c\n  PRIVATE_DEPS\n    spi_flash_reg\n)\n```",
